-- title:
--   Riemann–Siegel sample data, bands 320–327 (heights ≈92082.3715–≈92747.4441)
-- statement:
--   Riemann–Siegel sample data for the zeros of $\zeta(1/2+it)$, bands 320–327 of the extension from height $65000$ to $100000$ (heights $t\in[≈92082.3715,\,≈92747.4441]$).
--
--   Each band is a list of records of the structure `RS5.Sample` from the published framework: a dyadic height $t=tn/2^{16}$, a margin $E$ and integer hint fields for the Riemann–Siegel main sum. Consecutive bands share their endpoint sample, and each band has 128 samples (the last band of the range may be shorter).
--
--   The data were produced by a program and are not trusted. The problem `RH1E5.group_040` states that every band passes the kernel-evaluated sharp band checker of the framework, which certifies a sign change of Hardy's $Z(t)$ between consecutive samples of opposite sign.
-- source:
--   Computational certificate extending the kernel-checked verification of the Riemann hypothesis on prove2.me (published ArdaRH65K framework, Proved to height 65000) to height 100000; data produced by an exact integer Rust port of the framework checkers and checked by the Lean kernel.

